== what the nuclear magneton is
m_e from mu_B = e hbar / (2 m_e): 9.109383713937393e-31 kg ; m_p = m_e x (m_p/m_e): 1.672621925960941e-27 kg
mu_N = e hbar / (2 m_p) = 5.050783739238859e-27 J/T ;  mu_B / (m_p/m_e) = 5.0507837392388585e-27  (equal)
proton reduced Compton length hbar/(m_p c) = 2.1030891005002003e-16 m (the stack lists 2.1030891e-16)
e c lambda_p / 2 = 5.0507837392388585e-27 J/T ; ratio to mu_N = 0.9999999999999999  i.e. mu_N is the moment of one charge e circling at c on the radius lambda_p (current e c/(2 pi r) times area pi r^2)
mu_N / h = 7.622593218755553 MHz/T

