== symptoms: how the nucleus is not a point particle
Dirac point proton (g = 2, spin 1/2): mu = 1.0000 mu_N; measured 2.792847351 -> factor 2.792847351  (g_p = 5.5856947)
Dirac point neutron (no charge): mu = 0; measured -1.9130427 mu_N : a neutral particle with a moment must have charged parts that do not cancel
measured ratio mu_n / mu_p = -0.6849793273932501
quark picture (textbook, from memory): mu_p = (4 mu_u - mu_d)/3, mu_n = (4 mu_d - mu_u)/3, mu_q = e_q hbar/(2 m_q), m_q = m_p/3 gives mu_u = 2, mu_d = -1 (units mu_N): mu_p = 3.0000, mu_n = -2.0000, ratio -2/3 = -0.66667
   against measured 2.7928 (-6.9%), -1.9130 (-4.3%), ratio -0.68498

== symptoms in the gram: carbon-13 (natural abundance from the table row for carbon-12 = 98.94%, so 13C taken as 1.06%)
13C nuclei in one gram: 5.319557673171683e+20  moment each 3.5475139241454584e-27 J/T
all 13C moments aligned (expressed ceiling): M = 1.8871204915871361e-06 J/T
   in B = 1.0 T at T = 298.15 K: M = 1.6263e-12 J/T ; manifest/expressed = tanh(8.618e-07) = 8.6180e-07
   in B = 1.0 T at T = 4.2 K: M = 1.1545e-10 J/T ; manifest/expressed = tanh(6.118e-05) = 6.1177e-05
nuclear Curie mass susceptibility of the 13C moments, 298.15 K: 2.0437e-15 m^3/kg = 1.6263e-13 emu/g (cgs: x 1e3/(4 pi))
compare the diamond orbital (diamagnetic) susceptibility -4.9e-7 cm^3/g (secondary table value, unverified, carbon_aspect_sourced_values.txt section 3): ratio nuclear/diamagnetic = 3.32e-07

== ablating the size scaling in the instrument against the measured moment ratio (proton order over electron order)
instrument: moment per charge ratio = rho_p^(2g-1), rho_p = 1/(m_p/m_e), edge scaling geo = rho^g (g = 0: size does not follow the tick; g = 1: size follows the tick, the lab anchor)
       g    model ratio   model/measured |mu_p/mu_e|    model/(mu_N/mu_B)
   0.000   1.836153e+03                 1.208575e+06         3.371457e+06
   0.500   1.000000e+00                 6.582107e+02         1.836153e+03
   0.750   2.333703e-02                 1.536068e+01         4.285035e+01
   1.000   5.446170e-04                 3.584727e-01         1.000000e+00
   1.250   1.270974e-05                 8.365690e-03         2.333703e-02
   1.500   2.966077e-07                 1.952304e-04         5.446170e-04
   2.000   1.615376e-10                 1.063258e-07         2.966077e-07
exponent that reproduces the measured |mu_p/mu_e| exactly: g = 0.931746888763938 ; the one that reproduces mu_N/mu_B: g = 1.0
the difference 1 - g = 0.06825311123606204  is ln(mu_p/mu_N) / (2 ln(m_p/m_e)) =  0.06833021797878872
